{"_id":"6966313a3eeddc26d7c3a5a2","roadmapSlug":"ruby","nodeId":"aLIXcqB258WNrdASuN_7G","description":"# Floats\n\nFloats represent real numbers with fractional parts in Ruby. They are used to store numerical values that require more precision than integers can provide. Floats are typically represented using a decimal point or in scientific notation.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"class Floar","url":"https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/Float.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd842"},{"type":"article","title":"Numbers","url":"https://ruby-for-beginners.rubymonstas.org/built_in_classes/numbers.html","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd843"},{"type":"article","title":"Numbers - Odin Project","url":"https://www.theodinproject.com/lessons/ruby-basic-data-types#numbers","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd844"},{"type":"video","title":"03 Ruby Learning Path Integers and Floats","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FScOX-TavfA","_id":"6a7f4b2bcb44947debcfd845"}],"createdAt":"2026-01-13T11:49:14.128Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:06:51.273Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/ruby/content/aLIXcqB258WNrdASuN_7G.md"}